{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q134958756","formula":"C₁₂H₁₇NO₂","hill":"C12H17NO2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":12.0,"H":17.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"DOM-CR"},"descriptions":{"en":"DOM-CR, or DOM/CR, an acronym of \"DOM-conformationally restrained\", is a tetrahydroisoquinoline (THIQ) and cyclized phenethylamine related to the psychedelics DOM and 2C-D. It is a cyclized THIQ analogue of DOM and 2C-D. DOM-CR shows more than 20-fold reduced affinity for the serotonin 5-HT2A receptor compared to DOM (Ki = 2,150 nM vs. 100 nM, respectively). In contrast to DOM, DOM-CR does not substitute for DOM in rodent drug discrimination tests, suggesting that it lacks psychedelic effects."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":10198181,"mass":207.27,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC1=CC(=C2CCNCC2=C1OC)OC","inchikey":"LDSXYNSFNYUAHP-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"5,8-dimethoxy-7-methyl-1,2,3,4-tetrahydroisoquinoline","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"10198181","atoms":32,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.66,"y":0.513,"z":0.43,"el":"O"},{"x":2.254,"y":-1.823,"z":-0.489,"el":"O"},{"x":0.847,"y":2.94,"z":0.516,"el":"N"},{"x":0.955,"y":0.17,"z":-0.138,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.294,"y":0.761,"z":0.121,"el":"C"},{"x":2.196,"y":1.023,"z":-0.215,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.423,"y":2.26,"z":0.236,"el":"C"},{"x":1.879,"y":2.505,"z":-0.424,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.435,"y":-0.048,"z":0.211,"el":"C"},{"x":1.051,"y":-1.221,"z":-0.266,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.331,"y":-1.432,"z":0.072,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.089,"y":-2.018,"z":-0.164,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.539,"y":-2.304,"z":0.172,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.414,"y":0.885,"z":-0.721,"el":"C"},{"x":3.005,"y":-2.212,"z":0.659,"el":"C"},{"x":2.754,"y":0.906,"z":0.722,"el":"H"},{"x":2.838,"y":0.687,"z":-1.037,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.845,"y":2.654,"z":-0.697,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.112,"y":2.511,"z":1.05,"el